SDK guest clock: carry fractional guest ticks between UpdateGuestClock calls.
Phase B item B6 (docs/sdk-from-source.md). Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py
(SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). Without it the scaled clock path ran ~0.96x real time on
Apple Silicon (24 MHz host, ratio 25/12; movie audio starvation), because each host
tick delta was converted with truncating integer math and the remainder dropped.
Two more fixes in the same function, needed for an exact clock once all callers
use it: last_host_tick_count_ never moves backwards (a thread that read the host
clock before another thread's update could take the lock after it and rewind it,
so the next update counted that interval twice: +0.03-0.08% at 2x turbo), and a
ratio change first counts the time since the last update at the old ratio.
Also defines REX_CLOCK_EXACT_GUEST_TICKS in clock.h. The executable's old override
(src/core/fable2_guest_clock.h, a strong Clock::QueryGuestTickCount with an anchored
exact count) is compiled out when that macro exists, so every caller, recompiled mftb
sites included, reads this runtime clock. It stays the fallback on the prebuilt runtime.

